From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:51:18 +0900
Subject: Label every error and warning with its bolt code under -Zbolt-codes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A bolt code names a diagnostic in one form across Propensive's projects:
↯/p.1.7 is Proscala's subdivision 1, error 7. Subdivision 1 is upstream's
own numbering, so E007 is ↯/p.1.7. A message upstream leaves unnumbered is
known by the template of the em"..." string that made it, which the
interpolator now records, and whose code is looked up in the registry the
build puts in the compiler's jar. A message reported by a macro is ↯/p.2.2,
and carries the macro's own bolt code if its text began with one, as the
compound ↯/p.2.2/s.87.1.2.

The code replaces upstream's number in the console heading, and is given
to semdiag's XML, sbt's bridge and the presentation compiler.

Written with the assistance of Claude (an LLM).

Proscala-Patch: boltcodes
